# A colossus TAKES A STEP, watched in real seconds (src/systems/19_colossi.gd).
# The looming walker is staged alone a few world minutes before it lifts its
# leading foot, and the eye stands looking at that foot: a frame every fifteen
# seconds for the two minutes the swing takes, so the foot is seen to lift
# straight up out of the haze, be carried, and set down slowly. The walk is the
# world clock itself (colossus_walk.gd), so this is the real pace and not a
# sped-up one.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/colossi_stride.tour --seed=7 --place=coast --hour=12 --colossus=1@725 --face=353 --eye=1.7,-8 --weather=clear:0
wait 8
shot stride-00
wait 15
shot stride-01
wait 15
shot stride-02
wait 15
shot stride-03
wait 15
shot stride-04
wait 15
shot stride-05
wait 15
shot stride-06
wait 15
shot stride-07
wait 15
shot stride-08
wait 15
shot stride-09
